  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conflict Mitigation and Community Reconciliation in Northwest Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration (IOM), Mercy Corps (MC), and the Centre for Democracy and Development (CDD) will partner to implement a comprehensive pilot programme to reduce community violence in Batsari, Jibia, Dan Musa, and Kankara Local Government Areas (LGA) in Katsina State in Northwest region of Nigeria. The project seeks to strengthen peacebuilding processes to support the implementation of political and community responses to violence and strengthen the governance system to promote social cohesion and address the needs and grievances of communities. The project will establish and strengthen the local peace structures to provide citizens with a space to facilitate inclusive and participatory approaches to finding solutions to inter and intra-communal conflicts.</narrative>
  </description>
